<p>Sizes above use decimal GB. The shared <a href="./drama3_codec.safetensors">drama3_codec.safetensors</a> adds <strong>1.57 GB</strong> and works with either quant.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Q2_K:</strong> the smallest option; about <strong>16.2% smaller</strong> than Q3_K. Choose it when download size or system RAM is the priority.</li>
<li><strong>Q3_K:</strong> retains more expert precision and had lower sampled weight error. Choose it when you can accommodate the larger file; listen to both with your own prompts and reference voices.</li>
</ul>
<p>The quant names describe the <strong>routed experts</strong>, not every tensor in the model. All <strong>752 non-expert tensors</strong> retain their original dtypes and values, byte for byte between these builds. These include the shared experts, routers, attention/DeltaNet layers, embeddings, compact audio head, and audio tower. The codec is shared and unchanged between the quants.</p>
<p>Both builds were quantized directly from FP32 reconstructions of the official block-FP8 experts using GGML&#39;s reference encoders. Q2_K was not made by requantizing Q3_K or W4A8.</p>
</section>
<section class="d3-section" id="how-the-custom-nodes-work"><span class="d3-section-no">02 / DOCUMENTATION</span><h2>How the custom nodes work</h2><p>The updated ComfyUI-Drama3 loader recognizes the packed Q2_K and Q3_K expert tensors. Experts remain packed in <strong>pinned system RAM</strong>, and a bounded LRU cache keeps recently used packed experts on the GPU. CUDA generation reads the packed blocks through <strong>fused Triton kernels</strong>; prefill expands the expert being processed to BF16.</p>
<p>Both quants use the same <strong>Load Drama 3</strong>, voice, generation, and codec nodes. Existing upstream node IDs are retained, and the bundle also retains support for the corrected W4A8 build.</p>
<p>These are <strong>ComfyUI <code>.safetensors</code> models</strong> using GGML K-quant block layouts. They require the included K-quant integration; GGUF, llama.cpp, audio.cpp, and a Transformers pipeline are not the inference path for these files.</p>
</section>
<section class="d3-section" id="installation"><span class="d3-section-no">03 / DOCUMENTATION</span><h2>Installation</h2><div class="d3-note"><p><strong>Validated path:</strong> Linux + NVIDIA CUDA + Triton. Use the Python environment that runs ComfyUI.</p></div><p>Use an existing working ComfyUI installation. <strong>Linux, NVIDIA CUDA, and Triton</strong> are the validated execution path. Install or check dependencies using the Python environment that runs ComfyUI.</p>
<h3>Fresh node installation</h3>
<ol>
<li>Stop ComfyUI completely.</li>
<li>Download <a href="./ComfyUI-Drama3-KQuants.zip">ComfyUI-Drama3-KQuants.zip</a> and extract it into <code>ComfyUI/custom_nodes/</code>. The archive contains the complete <code>ComfyUI-Drama3/</code> source folder, including K-quant support.</li>
<li>If a <code>ComfyUI-Drama3</code> folder is already present, move it to a backup <strong>outside <code>custom_nodes</code></strong> first. Keep only one active copy to avoid duplicate node registration.</li>
<li>Place your chosen model and the shared codec as shown below. Download both model files only if you want to switch between quants.</li>
<li>Restart ComfyUI completely.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code class="language-text">ComfyUI/
├── custom_nodes/
│   └── ComfyUI-Drama3/
├── models/
│   ├── diffusion_models/
│   │   ├── drama3_q2_k_experts_bf16.safetensors
│   │   └── drama3_q3_k_experts_bf16.safetensors
│   └── vae/
│       └── drama3_codec.safetensors
└── output/
    └── drama3_voices/
        └── synthetic_voice.safetensors  # optional test reference
</code></pre>
<p>If you already have the compatible Drama 3 codec, reuse it.</p>
</section>
<section class="d3-section" id="first-generation"><span class="d3-section-no">04 / DOCUMENTATION</span><h2>First generation</h2><p>For a quick test, download <a href="./comfy_q2_workflow.json">comfy_q2_workflow.json</a> and <a href="./synthetic_voice.safetensors">synthetic_voice.safetensors</a>. Place the voice file in <code>ComfyUI/output/drama3_voices/</code>, then drag the workflow into ComfyUI. The reference voice was generated synthetically for validation.</p>
<p>In <strong>Load Drama 3</strong>, select either model and use:</p>
<div class="d3-table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Setting</th>
<th>Starting value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><code>experts</code></td>
<td><strong>in RAM</strong> — required for Q2_K/Q3_K</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>expert_cache_gb</code></td>
<td><strong>8</strong> — the measured cache size, in GiB</td>
</tr>
