<section class="d3-section" id="troubleshooting"><span class="d3-section-no">07 / DOCUMENTATION</span><h2>Troubleshooting</h2><div class="d3-table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Symptom</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><code>disable_weight_init has no attribute MoEExperts</code></td>
<td>Install the K-quant node bundle or focused loader patch, then restart ComfyUI completely. The standard loader does not recognize these packed experts.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Q2_K / Q3_K CUDA execution requires Triton</code></td>
<td>Check that Triton is available in the Python environment actually running ComfyUI. Linux CUDA is the tested path.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Error about experts in RAM or a second GPU</td>
<td>Set <code>experts = in RAM</code> and <code>second_gpu = none</code>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CUDA out of memory</td>
<td>Lower <code>expert_cache_gb</code> and account for other models using VRAM. The cache is only part of the GPU allocation.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Voice file is missing from the dropdown</td>
<td>Put the saved voice in <code>output/drama3_voices/</code> and refresh the file list.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Silent or incomplete speech</td>
<td>Check that the reference transcript covers the clip exactly, use clean speech cut between sentences, and try another seed or reference. Keep the starting sampling settings above.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Duplicate nodes after installation</td>
<td>Keep one active <code>ComfyUI-Drama3</code> folder. Move backups outside <code>custom_nodes</code>.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table></div>
